<title>USA: Boeing confirms order talks with USAir.</title>
<headline>Boeing confirms order talks with USAir.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co confirmed Monday that it is bidding for a potentially major order for new jets from USAir Group Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;We are in discusssions with USAir regarding their fleet requirements,&quot; said Boeing spokeswoman Barbara Murphy. She said any order announcements would be up to the airline.</p>
<p>Earlier the Wall Street Journal reported that USAir is considering buying up to 120 jets worth more than $5 billion and is in talks with Boeing, Airbus Industrie and McDonnell Douglas Corp.</p>
<p>					-- Seattle bureau 206-386-4848</p>
</text>
